+lines as well, with their own amounts and the rate charged. Amounts, on the
+record and on each line (`discount`, `net`, `tax`, `total`), are integers in the
+currency's minor units: `1234` is $12.34, ¥1,234 or KD 1.234. A line's
+`quantity` is a decimal string such as `"1.5"`, and its `unit_price` and
+`rate` are decimal strings too.
 
 | Field | JSON type | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
 | `record.number` | `string` | Invoice number. |
 | `record.region` | `string` | Normalised region code. |
 | `record.currency` | `string` | ISO 4217 code. |
-| `record.subtotal` | `string` | Sum of line amounts before discounts, as a decimal. |
-| `record.discount` | `string` | Total discount, as a decimal. |
-| `record.tax` | `string` | Total tax, as a decimal. |
-| `record.total` | `string` | Amount due, as a decimal. |
+| `record.subtotal` | `integer` | Sum of line amounts before discounts, in minor units. |
+| `record.discount` | `integer` | Total discount, in minor units. |
+| `record.tax` | `integer` | Total tax, in minor units. |
+| `record.total` | `integer` | Amount due, in minor units. |
 | `record.lines` | `array` | One object per line item. |
 
